1786479936602484	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy3RU		item.create	bn-39zu	{"description":"# Field report (continuum, 2026-08-11): dirty-trunk preserve/replay during merge dropped recent appends to an uncommitted tracked file\n\nReported by continuum-dev on #maw (msg 01KZRMBJ61Z8MMDDBDXKMAB4GR). Tracking bone in continuum: bn-2rb1c.\n\n## Observed\n\n- continuum's `.bones/events/2026-08.events` (uncommitted tracked trunk file, append-only) lost all events for bone bn-31cq1 (created/labeled/commented/closed 2026-08-09, all writes returned ok=true).\n- By 2026-08-11 `bn show bn-31cq1` returns item-not-found; the shard contains ZERO bn-31cq1 events from 2026-08-09.\n- On 2026-08-09 several `maw ws merge` runs printed: `uncommitted tracked trunk file(s) preserved and replayed (recovery snapshot pinned): .bones/events/2026-08.events`.\n- One of those merges (continuum bn-3bn62 @ 6408b682) ran with trunk one commit AHEAD of the epoch.\n- Blast radius narrow: every other bone from that window still resolves.\n\n## Hypothesis (continuum-dev's, plausible)\n\nThe preserve/replay path restored the dirty file from a snapshot that PREDATED recent appends — i.e. the snapshot was captured earlier (or against a stale base), and replaying it over the post-merge tree overwrote appends that landed between snapshot capture and restore. The trunk-ahead-of-epoch merge is the prime suspect: content diffing against the epoch instead of trunk HEAD's actual tree could misclassify or resurrect an older version of the file.\n\n## Where to look\n\n- The dirty-trunk preservation path in merge (the code that prints \"preserved and replayed (recovery snapshot pinned)\") — snapshot capture timing vs restore timing, and what base it diffs against when trunk != epoch.\n- bn-1xmk (pre.10 trunk dirty-file data-loss fix) and bn-2bcx DST DirtyTrunkWrite escape op — this may be a surviving corner (trunk committed-ahead + dirty same file + multiple merges same day).\n- Evidence is local: ~/src/continuum (shard at .bones/events/2026-08.events, recovery refs refs/manifold/recovery/*, merge commits from 2026-08-09).\n\n## Goal\n\n1. Reproduce: trunk one commit ahead of epoch + uncommitted tracked file appended-to after some earlier merge snapshot, then merge; verify appends survive.\n2. Fix so preserve/replay never restores content older than the file's bytes at merge start.\n3. DST oracle: dirty trunk file bytes at merge start must be a prefix/subset of bytes after merge (append-only preservation).\n4. Check continuum's recovery refs — the lost events may still be recoverable from a pinned snapshot; if so, tell continuum-dev how.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["field-report"],"title":"Merge dirty-trunk preserve/replay can restore stale snapshot, dropping recent appends (continuum field report)"}	blake3:vylbKW3r-2W655ESv0NBq6xnLegbD2TvrzZdiRHfHo4
1786479936764280	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy3hU		item.create	bn-1du0	{"description":"# Field report (continuum, 2026-08-11): merge engine reverted/dropped Cargo.lock hunks on two consecutive merges\n\nReported by continuum-dev on #maw (msg 01KZRRD0QDDQE7Q14FQ9H6QJRW). Tracking bone in continuum: bn-doim5. Two failures in OPPOSITE directions on the same file, same day.\n\n## Case 1 — merge wrote an INTERMEDIATE epoch's content (continuum bn-ymw, merge c011608)\n\n- Workspace tree at merge time verifiably had blake3 1.8.5 / cc 1.4.0 / find-msvc-tools 0.1.9 (`git diff f69944b -- Cargo.lock` = 4 insertions 0 deletions; audit script passed IN the workspace).\n- Merge commit nevertheless wrote 1.8.6 / 1.4.2 / 0.1.10 to trunk — the values from epoch b0a8569, an intermediate state the workspace had been rebased THROUGH earlier and then rebased off.\n- Net effect: reverted trunk fix f69944b.\n- Caveat: this workspace had been recovered from a snapshot and manually rebased with raw git before `maw ws sync` — maw's recorded base may have been stale.\n\n## Case 2 — merge silently DROPPED the workspace's hunk (continuum bn-3tz3, merge 3690dbb)\n\n- Workspace carried an explicit 12-line Cargo.lock change against base 93f0623.\n- Merge commit contains NO Cargo.lock hunk at all. Silently dropped.\n- This workspace was created normally and synced only via `maw ws sync` — the stale-manual-rebase explanation does NOT cover this case.\n\n## Suspected mechanism (unconfirmed)\n\nMerge engine resolves (at least this path) against a recorded base or an intermediate epoch rather than the workspace's current tree. Possible interaction with auto_resolve/lockfile-special-casing or with the recorded epoch/base metadata surviving rebases.\n\n## Impact at continuum\n\nTrunk dependency-audit gate goes red for every worker after each occurrence; third and fourth lockfile-drift-to-trunk incidents (first two were non---locked cargo calls; these two are maw's doing).\n\n## Where to look\n\n- Merge base selection: what does the engine use as base when the workspace has been rebased (manually or via sync) — recorded epoch metadata vs merge-base of actual trees?\n- Any Cargo.lock/lockfile special-casing in the conflict engine or auto-resolve.\n- Evidence is local: ~/src/continuum, merge commits c011608 and 3690dbb, bases f69944b / b0a8569 / 93f0623.\n\n## Goal\n\n1. From the continuum repo, reconstruct both merges (workspace recovery snapshots should still exist) and determine the actual base/content-resolution each used.\n2. Reproduce minimally; fix; DST coverage (workspace-modified file must appear in merge result unless conflicting; merge result for a path must never equal an intermediate epoch's content when both endpoints agree otherwise).\n","kind":"bug","labels":["field-report"],"title":"Merge engine reverted/dropped Cargo.lock hunks vs workspace tree (continuum field report)"}	blake3:QRXIL9-umJdIEtVeH-K_IDa0njcN0Yctahb9qlFAgTs
1786480883526334	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy3xU		item.comment	bn-39zu	{"body":"ROOT CAUSE FOUND (2026-08-11 forensics in ~/src/continuum). maw's preserve/replay is EXONERATED. The loss did not happen in the dirty-trunk snapshot path. Sequence: (1) bn-2phq3 workspace held a stale copy of .bones/events/2026-08.events; commit 9c040db (17:37:58 local, post-sync) still had the correct 1220-line file. (2) Between 17:37:58 and 17:39:21 something IN the workspace rewrote the shard on disk back to stale 1200-line content (suspect: continuum regen tooling writing from a stale projection). (3) An agent committed all dirty files as 'chore: workspace regen artifacts (bn-2phq3)' (unreachable commit 9435ebd) — that commit itself deletes the 20 events. (4) maw ws sync replayed it faithfully (273833c) and merge 1514d0c published it. Every snapshot along the way is intact; the 20 events survive in trunk commit a4e905a and in refs/manifold/recovery/default/2026-08-09T21-39-32Z. The dirty-file replay correctly carried the 4 uncommitted appends forward (diff-and-reapply), which is why post-merge working copies show 'block missing, later appends intact'. Continuum's snapshot-predating-appends hypothesis is disproven. REMAINING maw ACTION (this bone's new scope): hardening — a merge that applies a source-workspace change which is a pure REWIND of a path to an older epoch's blob (or deletes lines from a configured append-only path) should warn or require --force. That guard would have caught this."}	blake3:UN5kyMyyyns5c3FRvBlCeJwuH8axJhLQ8wrNYCTVSy0
1786480883553664	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy4BU		item.comment	bn-1du0	{"body":"ROOT CAUSE FOUND (2026-08-11 forensics in ~/src/continuum): maw's DEFAULT merge driver for Cargo.lock (crates/maw-core/src/config.rs default_merge_drivers: match=Cargo.lock, kind=Regenerate, command='cargo generate-lockfile', required=false) fires for BOTH unique and shared paths (apply_merge_drivers loops partition.unique too). cargo generate-lockfile re-resolves every dependency to the newest compatible version, discarding deliberate lock pins that BOTH sides agreed on. Proof in continuum odb: for each affected merge the engine first built a provisional candidate with the CORRECT content (bn-ymw: e39b8ba/fb8c7ee; bn-3tz3: 72b1be3/f3ce1bf, all 'epoch: merge' commits), then the regenerate driver overwrote the path and the published merge (c011608, 3690dbb) carries the regenerated (drifted) lockfile. The 'intermediate epoch b0a8569 values' were coincidence: that lock had itself been regenerated, so fresh-resolve output matched it. Note maw hit this same class itself (bn-496a lockfile regeneration during merge). RECOMMENDED FIX: (1) only fire regenerate drivers when textual resolution actually CONFLICTS — never on unique paths (take source verbatim) and never when diff3 merges cleanly; (2) print a NOTE naming every path a driver rewrote (currently silent); (3) consider a conservative regen command or config to disable defaults. Regression tests: unique-path lockfile change must survive byte-identical; cleanly-merging shared lockfile edits must survive."}	blake3:t8hNTvf_6BOEQsRSil_floUsBb51EGuUMD0A7jAWHY4
1786548009413025	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy4RU		item.create	bn-p3m9	{"description":"# Field report 3 (continuum, 2026-08-11): fresh workspaces materialized with working-tree reverts of a recent trunk commit\n\nReported on #maw (msg 01KZS9Q4EXNTFWYKH5CZ9F6FPV). Continuum tracking: bn-doim5 (comment 1). maw = 1.0.0-pre.13.\n\n## Confirmed signature (forensics in ~/src/continuum)\n\nTwo workspaces (bn-3huh7, bn-16v3x), independently, within the same minutes:\n- HEAD and index at ea85bf6 (trunk tip).\n- Working tree = ea85bf6 checkout EXCEPT exactly the 7 paths touched by 613d8fa (ea85bf6's parent), which carry BYTE-EXACT 96a1fe7 blobs (613d8fa's parent = the then-stale epoch ref value). Verified: dropped-stash commits c1258c6 / 8d73965 (unreachable, recovered) diff vs ea85bf6 = exact inverse of 613d8fa (22+/45-), and blob OIDs equal 96a1fe7's.\n- git status showed the 7 files as local modifications (reverts); workers stashed them.\n\n## Reconstructed timeline (UTC 2026-08-11)\n\n- 20:09:31 merge bn-37o0d -> epoch 96a1fe7.\n- 20:15:33 trunk-direct 613d8fa (close/regen, commits the 7 files); lead ran `maw epoch sync` -> epoch 613d8fa (PROVEN: unreachable cbe5b1b = pre-merge sync of bn-3j01v replayed onto 613d8fa at 20:26:29).\n- 20:23:19 trunk-direct ea85bf6 (edict-hook commit) — never epoch-synced.\n- Fresh workspaces created --from main in ~20:23-20:26 (HEAD ea85bf6).\n- 20:26:32 merge bn-3j01v: reconcile absorbed epoch to ea85bf6, merged -> 733b0fa. Its AUTO-REBASE left both fresh workspaces at ea85bf6 => they were ALREADY DIRTY (poisoned) by 20:26:35.\n- 20:28:10 / 20:32:17 workers found + stashed the reverts.\n\nThe two content sources of the poison (96a1fe7 blobs; path set = 613d8fa's diff) are exactly the epoch ref's two historical values — some worktree-materialization path is keyed off stale epoch state instead of the checkout target.\n\n## NOT reproduced by (all clean, maw pre.13, 7 repro variants in scratchpad)\n\n1. `ws create --from main` with epoch ref stale-behind by 2 (clean-room). \n2. `ws sync` forward and backward (backward: ancestor-refusal guard works; 'up to date' otherwise).\n3. `ws advance` (refuses ephemeral).\n4. Merge with dirty trunk + FF-absorb, siblings at old epoch / at intermediate commit B / at tip C; with prior merge writing epoch/ws/default; dirty files overlapping B's commit.\n5. The EXACT reconstructed op sequence: epoch sync to B -> trunk commit C -> creates -> lead `ws sync source` (replays onto B, matches cbe5b1b) -> merge (absorb B..C).\n6. 5x concurrency stress: parallel creates racing sync+merge.\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- Any path that writes epoch/anchor blobs into worktrees: `replay_snapshot_with_merge_protection` (working_copy.rs ~879, delete/modify branch writes anchor content), rebase.rs epoch-delta three-way (~1568+, ref_old side), ff_absorb FF-materialize path.\n- Get worker command logs from continuum for 20:23-20:28Z: which maw/git commands ran inside bn-3huh7 between create and first status (requested on-channel).\n- The workers' edict/protocol-start tooling may run maw commands we haven't modeled.\n\n## Defense regardless of mechanism (recommend implementing now)\n\nAfter create / sync / FF-absorb / auto-rebase, for a workspace that should be clean: assert worktree == HEAD tree (fast status check already exists) and WARN loudly + auto-repair (checkout the delta) or refuse, instead of leaving silent divergence. This converts the whole class into a caught error. Add a DST oracle: post-materialization clean-workspace worktree must equal HEAD tree.\n\n## Impact\n\nWorking-tree-only corruption on fresh workspaces; committed state intact everywhere (Prime Invariant held). Blast radius: workers must notice unexplained local modifications or they commit reverts (bn-1du0-adjacent trunk regression risk).\n","kind":"bug","labels":["field-report"],"title":"Fresh workspaces materialized with stale-epoch blobs for a recent trunk commit's paths (continuum field report 3)"}	blake3:_xNfh1dM5lOQuHlSL8qZo3cnwOn7NMh50NvD2uf8q7M
1786550865479148	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy4hU		item.update	bn-39zu	{"field":"title","value":"Merge guard: warn/refuse when a source workspace change is a pure rewind of a path to an older epoch blob (from continuum field report 1)"}	blake3:bul-cBO7CRuYULn76w-Pu2M0QLzxTOi3F2a0dvGGL7Y
1786550865669926	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy4xU		item.create	bn-3gba	{"description":"# Mechanism-independent defense for the bn-p3m9 class (implementable NOW, does not wait for root cause)\n\nContext: bn-p3m9 (continuum field report 3) — fresh workspaces materialized with stale-epoch blobs on some paths while HEAD/index pointed at the right commit. Root cause not yet reproduced; this bone ships the defense that converts the whole class from silent corruption into a caught error.\n\n## Work items\n\n1. **Post-materialization verification**: after any operation that is supposed to leave a workspace clean at a known commit — `ws create`, `ws sync` (FF path), FF-absorb sibling fast-forward/replay, post-merge auto-rebase — run the existing cheap dirty check (`status_head_to_worktree`) and, if the worktree unexpectedly differs from the HEAD tree:\n   - print a loud WARNING naming the paths,\n   - auto-repair by checking out the divergent paths from HEAD (the workspace is supposed to be clean; content is recoverable by definition),\n   - record the event (oplog + artifacts) so field reports carry the evidence.\n   Skip the check when the operation intentionally preserves dirty state (snapshot/replay paths) — only assert where clean-at-commit is the contract.\n2. **DST oracle**: after every create/sync/absorb/auto-rebase op in the simulation, assert clean-workspace worktree tree hash == HEAD tree hash. This is the oracle that would have caught bn-p3m9 the day it shipped.\n3. Wire the new lane into `just check` / CI per the bn-1n2b convention.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A fault-injected partial materialization (write one stale blob into a fresh workspace mid-create, test-only failpoint) is detected, repaired, and reported.\n- DST default profile stays byte-identical unless the oracle fires (follow bn-2bcx's pattern for adding oracles without perturbing the soak).\n","kind":"task","labels":["field-report"],"title":"Post-materialization worktree==HEAD verification + DST oracle (defense for bn-p3m9 class)"}	blake3:XGuT3heBr3FnYQPtvNn5-FduxHRBWUvAyfcGRzrQYF4
1786550881425780	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy5BU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"Defense split out as bn-3gba (post-materialization worktree==HEAD verification + DST oracle) — implementable without the root cause. This bone stays open for the mechanism investigation, currently blocked on continuum-dev's worker command logs (channel anchor 01KZS9Q4EXNTFWYKH5CZ9F6FPV)."}	blake3:I0wMO0yggsLyZZh0TMM-DE-VyoUoY8vDbMg0JNWAH6Y
1786550881461045	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy5RU		item.comment	bn-3gba	{"body":"Origin: bn-p3m9 investigation. See that bone's dossier for the exact corruption signature the failpoint test should mimic (stale-epoch blobs on one commit's path set, HEAD/index correct)."}	blake3:rpSDm2Z8aZM6CeRxUI8bpR4aaM15-5czLzTX3VF9abk
1786552132962188	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy5hU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"continuum-dev supplied the requested data (2026-08-12): ZERO git/maw commands ran in bn-3huh7 between 'maw ws create --from main' and the worker's first 'git status' (89 intervening commands, all read-only file inspection). VECTOR CONFIRMED: create itself materialized the stale blobs. Clean-room still does not reproduce: repro7 shape (epoch synced to B, main at C, dirty trunk) + 3x concurrent creates — all clean on pre.13. Trigger is environment-scale (their repo: large odb, ~40 destroyed worktrees so worktree_prune churn on every create, possible responder-hook concurrency). Investigation continues; bn-3gba (post-create worktree==HEAD verify + repair + DST oracle) is now the priority fix — continuum-dev confirms it would catch the class."}	blake3:Pz_4CCJ8jTYwvRwP2FY7ode88ZLgq364qfKNk5Bc3L4
1786554989583324	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy5xU		item.move	bn-1du0	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:WgP6g05AhbmdKl5L9tWI1wGVWvDgulZhf40XjDJpxSU
