1786823569037884	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEymBY		item.comment	bn-2mio	{"body":"Fixed in workspace bn-2mio, commit bc71049b (uncommitted to trunk — not yet merged). crates/maw-git/src/worktree_impl.rs: added write_index_with_retry() wrapping gix::index::File::write() with bounded retry (6 attempts, doubling backoff 15/30/60/120/240ms, ~465ms total budget) that only retries gix::index::file::write::Error::AcquireLock — any other write error fails immediately as before. Applied to both index writes in worktree_add (primary write at the old ~line 120-126 site, and the LFS smudge post-pass rewrite, best-effort as before). On exhausted retries the error names the workspace and tells the user `maw ws create <name>` is safe to retry (confirmed against GitWorktreeBackend::create in crates/maw-core/src/backend/git.rs, which already cleans up the worktree dir on worktree_add failure and prunes the stale admin dir on the next create attempt). worktree_remove has no index-lock site, left untouched. Tests: worktree_add_retries_through_transient_index_lock_contention (background thread holds the real gix_lock index.lock for 60ms, worktree_add must transparently retry past it and succeed) and worktree_add_reports_actionable_error_when_index_lock_exhausted (lock held 900ms > retry budget, asserts the error names both the workspace and 'maw ws create'). Both pass; full maw-git suite green (47/47, excluding the pre-existing unrelated checkout_impl::tests::checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files git-2.55.0 --force flake already documented on bn-39zu as reproducing on trunk with zero changes). Full workspace 'just check' green, zero FAILED markers."}	blake3:zdtlPeuajBySWoKSCj6YowClu6-zqjAex2A_6o7crGE
1786823578154038	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEymRY		item.comment	bn-2r7a	{"body":"Fixed in workspace bn-2mio (both bones share the file, one commit), commit bc71049b (uncommitted to trunk — not yet merged). crates/maw-git/src/worktree_impl.rs: added describe_checkout_incompleteness(outcome) which inspects outcome.collisions, outcome.delayed_paths_unknown, and outcome.delayed_paths_unprocessed after the existing outcome.errors check in worktree_add. Any non-empty field now fails create loudly (GitError::BackendError), naming every offending path plus its io::ErrorKind for collisions, and tells the user to remove the worktree and retry `maw ws create <name>` — matching the existing outcome.errors error path's behavior (no extra cleanup added, since worktree_add's other error paths also don't self-clean; cleanup already happens one layer up in GitWorktreeBackend::create, confirmed by reading crates/maw-core/src/backend/git.rs). Scope note: only worktree_add's gix::worktree::state::checkout call was touched; checkout_impl.rs's separate checkout path was not in scope for this bone and was not modified. Test-forcing note: worktree_add always sets overwrite_existing:true, and gix's open_file()/try_op_or_unlink() unlinks+replaces any filesystem obstruction (existing file/dir) before re-attempting the write rather than surfacing it as a collision — so a real collision is only reachable via a genuine case-insensitive-FS path clash or a TOCTOU race, neither forceable deterministically on ext4/Linux (confirmed by reading gix-worktree-state 0.19.0's entry.rs/chunk.rs). Per the bone's own fallback guidance, went the outcome-construction route instead: describe_checkout_incompleteness is a pure function tested directly by constructing gix::worktree::state::checkout::Outcome/Collision values. Tests added: describe_checkout_incompleteness_is_none_for_clean_outcome, describe_checkout_incompleteness_names_colliding_paths, describe_checkout_incompleteness_names_unprocessed_delayed_paths, describe_checkout_incompleteness_names_unknown_delayed_paths, worktree_add_error_message_shape_matches_incompleteness_report (asserts the actual message format worktree_add builds from the helper's output). All pass; full maw-git suite green aside from the pre-existing unrelated checkout_impl.rs git-2.55.0 flake (documented on bn-39zu). Full workspace 'just check' green, zero FAILED markers."}	blake3:BM1MAVF2KTQMYL5KrO6l9PYO1f0sHTRvU3O7lfDg8yY
1786823624022730	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEymhY		item.create	bn-24xy	{"description":"Pre-existing test failure on trunk (verified 2026-08-15 on 52ed44b6 with zero changes): cargo test -p maw-git --lib checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files fails. Cause per bn-39zu-era notes: git 2.55.0 changed checkout --force semantics vs what the test asserts. Not a product bug as far as known — test/environment mismatch. Fix the test or the checkout_impl behavior after confirming which semantic maw wants. Noted independently by two workers (bn-39zu, bn-2mio sessions).","kind":"bug","title":"checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files fails under git 2.55 (--force semantics mismatch)"}	blake3:AT8tpckqEofuH_fmVA4ELhkK7HHCdqdq6NV58yAMSkg
1786823624056942	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEymxY		item.comment	bn-2mio	{"body":"Lead review of bc71049b (maw-dev): APPROVED. Typed AcquireLock-only retry (6 attempts, 15ms doubling backoff ~465ms budget) at both index-write sites; exhausted-retry error names workspace + safe retry command; describe_checkout_incompleteness promotes collisions/delayed-paths to hard error naming paths, matching existing outcome.errors cleanup semantics (cleanup owned by GitWorktreeBackend::create — verified claim). Collision unforceable on ext4 due to gix overwrite_existing unlink-and-retry (worker read gix 0.19 source; pure-function tests are the right fallback). Flake claim verified: checkout_detach test fails on unmodified trunk — filed separately."}	blake3:X0H6hv1L1ECl2PavJ3UtnsxsCR4zcKqNITJ2If5aEG8
1786823632547009	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEynBY		item.comment	bn-36id	{"body":"Fixed: refs_impl::atomic_ref_update now classifies gix CAS failures by TYPED error variant instead of Display-substring matching.\n\nRoot cause confirmed: gix::Repository::edit_references returns gix::reference::edit::Error, whose FileTransactionPrepare variant wraps gix::refs::file::transaction::prepare::Error (gix 0.72.1 / gix-ref 0.52.1, vendored source read under ~/.cargo/registry). That type carries three CAS-precondition-failure variants, all now mapped to GitError::RefConflict:\n- MustNotExist { full_name, .. } - create-only CAS failed (ref exists when it shouldn't)\n- ReferenceOutOfDate { full_name, .. } - expected-old-value CAS mismatch on an existing ref\n- MustExist { full_name, .. } - update required ref to already exist, but it was missing (never triggered by our own PreviousValue usage today, included for completeness/robustness)\n\nNew helper classify_edit_error() in crates/maw-git/src/refs_impl.rs matches on these typed variants and pulls the ref name straight from full_name (accurate per-failure, not just \"first edit in the batch\" like the old code). All non-CAS prepare/commit errors still fall through to GitError::BackendError. The dead substring list (\"existing object id\", \"MustExistAndMatch\", \"did not match\", \"mustNotExist\", \"MustNotExist\") is gone.\n\nmaw-core's map_git_error (crates/maw-core/src/refs.rs) already had a GitError::RefConflict arm as its first match - that's now the live path. Broadened its defensive BackendError-message rescue (kept only as a fallback for hypothetical future GitRepo impls / CLI-stderr shapes) to also recognize \"was not supposed to exist\" / \"was supposed to exist\", with a comment marking it as dead-in-practice-but-kept-defensive.\n\nUn-ignored atomic_ref_update_conflict (crates/maw-git/tests/integration_test.rs) and had to fix the test itself: it set new_oid equal to the ref's already-existing value, which gix treats as an idempotent no-op success (not a MustNotExist conflict) when existing.target == new. Changed it to write a genuinely different oid so the create-race is real. Also added atomic_ref_update_conflict_value_mismatch to cover the ReferenceOutOfDate shape (CAS mismatch on an existing ref), which had no test before. All three atomic_ref_update_* tests in that file pass now.\n\nAudited sibling #[ignore]s in the same file: read_index_fresh_repo and status_shows_untracked_file are ignored for unrelated pre-existing bugs (index-file-missing handling, untracked-file status mapping) - left alone, out of scope.\n\nSearched the crate for the same anti-pattern (.to_string().contains / message.contains on gix errors in classification paths). Found two more sites, both in maw-cli (outside refs_impl, noted per bone scope but NOT fixed):\n- crates/maw-cli/src/push.rs:320 - msg.contains(\"conflict\") || msg.contains(\"lock\") || msg.contains(\"expected\") on atomic_ref_update's error in the epoch-advance path.\n- crates/maw-cli/src/release.rs:294-297 - msg.contains(\"conflict\") || msg.contains(\"exists\") || msg.contains(\"expected\") || msg.contains(\"MustNotExist\") on atomic_ref_update's error in the tag-creation race-retry path.\nBoth happen to keep working after this fix (GitError::RefConflict's own Display always starts with the literal string \"ref conflict on ...\", so .contains(\"conflict\") reliably fires), but they're the same fragile substring-matching-a-Display-string pattern and should eventually be converted to matches!(err, GitError::RefConflict { .. }).\n\nEvidence:\n- cargo test -p maw-git --test integration_test atomic_ref_update -> 3 passed (atomic_ref_update_success, atomic_ref_update_conflict, atomic_ref_update_conflict_value_mismatch), 0 failed.\n- cargo test -p maw-git (full crate) -> 39/40 pass; the 1 failure (checkout_impl::tests::checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files) is pre-existing and unrelated: reproduced with plain `git worktree add --force --detach <path>` outside any maw code - git 2.55 refuses to reuse an already-registered worktree path even with --force. File untouched by this change. Not fixed here (out of scope for bn-36id); may warrant its own bone.\n- just check (fmt, clippy -D warnings, full cargo test + cargo test -p maw-cli, DST g1-g4 + determinism, contract-drift) -> exit 0, 89/89 \"test result: ok\" blocks, 0 FAILED, 0 error lines. Note: this workspace-level test recipe doesn't invoke -p maw-git directly (only root package + maw-cli), so the maw-git crate-local tests above were verified separately.\n\nCommitted to workspace bn-36id at a2eb381b: \"fix: classify gix CAS failures by typed error variant (bn-36id)\". Workspace left open per instructions (not merged, not destroyed)."}	blake3:TLHNlh4cKsc5tSHOqcHoGlN1vibxRGkdgXLT3pVJqoc
1786823664119644	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEynRY		item.create	bn-2gbv	{"description":"Follow-up from bn-36id (2026-08-15): crates/maw-cli/src/push.rs:320 and crates/maw-cli/src/release.rs:294-297 do msg.contains('conflict')-style checks on atomic_ref_update errors. Still functionally correct post-bn-36id (RefConflict Display contains 'conflict') but same fragile pattern bn-36id removed from maw-git. Convert to matches!(err, GitError::RefConflict { .. }) — needs error to flow as GitError not anyhow string at those sites.","kind":"task","title":"push.rs/release.rs classify ref errors by Display substring instead of matches!(GitError::RefConflict)"}	blake3:pw3j5u_zZh6KkFWNSaDf7LUEfLLYZp4RO7jC6GFgH9s
1786823664150189	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEynhY		item.comment	bn-36id	{"body":"Lead review of a2eb381b (maw-dev): APPROVED. classify_edit_error matches typed PrepareError::MustNotExist/ReferenceOutOfDate/MustExist variants with per-failure full_name (better than the old first-edit guess); substring rescue retained only as documented fallback in maw-core map_git_error. Un-ignored test was itself buggy (same-oid = gix idempotent no-op, not a conflict) — fixed + new value-mismatch coverage. Flake claim matches bn-24xy (verified pre-existing on trunk). push.rs/release.rs substring sites filed as follow-up."}	blake3:P8g5Ayt4csJHy4kVV5Ii3q81SdzoBhLqKRKNBDzjxdk
1786824020375428	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEynxY		item.comment	bn-17o1	{"body":"Fixed: crates/maw-git/src/stash_impl.rs worktree_state_commit now writes blobs via the clean-filter-aware repo.write_blob_with_path(&data, &entry.path) trait method (crate::repo::GitRepo) instead of the raw crate::objects_impl::write_blob. This is the same write path used by the merge engine (crates/maw-core/src/merge/build.rs write_blob_at, crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs patch_candidate_tree) and rebase (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/sync/rebase.rs). LFS-tracked paths in a worktree snapshot now materialize as pointer blobs matching 'git stash create' / 'git add' semantics, instead of storing full file content.\n\nAudit of stash_impl.rs: only one raw write_blob call existed in the file (the one fixed above, inside worktree_state_commit's per-entry loop). stash_create doesn't hash content itself (it builds a tree from existing index entries, which already carry post-clean-filter oids from 'git add'). stash_apply only reads blobs to materialize the worktree — writing raw content there matches git's own smudge-filter gap in this codebase (no smudge filtering is implemented anywhere in maw-git; out of scope for this bone).\n\nOther raw write_blob call sites found elsewhere in the codebase (noted, not fixed — out of scope): crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs:6062/6071/6996 write raw metadata/epoch blobs (not user file content), crates/maw-core/src/oplog/write.rs:173 writes oplog JSON, crates/maw-core/src/merge/materialize.rs:1319 is test code. None of these represent user file content going through a clean filter, so they're a different risk class than stash_impl.\n\nPerformance note (item 3 in the bone): write_blob_with_path is NOT a cheap no-op in the no-filter case. Its internal AttrsMatcher::from_gix_head (crates/maw-lfs/src/attrs.rs) does a full recursive walk of the HEAD tree via gix object reads to find .gitattributes files, on every call, regardless of whether any filters are configured. worktree_state_commit calls it once per changed/added/untracked status entry, so a snapshot with N dirty files now pays N HEAD-tree walks. This is a pre-existing characteristic of write_blob_with_path already accepted elsewhere in the codebase (crates/maw-core/src/merge/build.rs write_blob_at and crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs patch_candidate_tree both call it in per-file loops with no caching), so this fix doesn't introduce a new performance class, but it does extend the existing cost to the stash/snapshot hot path. Flagging as a possible follow-up (cache the AttrsMatcher per worktree_state_commit call / per repo generation) if snapshot latency on large-changeset repos becomes a concern.\n\nTest added: crates/maw-git/src/stash_impl.rs stash_impl::tests::worktree_state_commit_writes_lfs_pointer_for_tracked_path (gated #[cfg(feature = \"lfs\")]) — commits a .gitattributes with '*.bin filter=lfs', dirties an untracked data.bin with raw content, calls worktree_state_commit, reads the resulting commit's tree entry for data.bin via read_blob_at_path, and asserts: it parses as a valid maw_lfs::Pointer (not the raw bytes), and the real content is retrievable from the LFS object store (maw_lfs::Store::open) by the pointer's sha256 oid.\n\nExisting regression tests green: stash_impl::tests::stash_apply_creates_symlinks_not_regular_files, stash_impl::tests::stash_apply_does_not_follow_existing_symlinks (no-filter path, unaffected).\n\nFull 'just check' run clean (exit 0, 0 test result: FAILED across the whole workspace including maw-git, maw-core, maw-cli, DST harness, contract_drift). Pre-existing unrelated flake noted but not touched: checkout_impl::tests::checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files fails intermittently on trunk too (tmp worktree path collision, unrelated to this bone) — reproduced identically on trunk at repo root with none of this bone's changes present.\n\nCommit: d8e31eed on the bn-17o1 workspace branch (not merged, not pushed)."}	blake3:ZR7j4HwDyaK_2TGF1Felr6mMoHLJLerNJeezPRE-yYI
1786824054528787	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyoBY		item.create	bn-2fps	{"description":"Follow-up from bn-17o1 (2026-08-15): maw_lfs::AttrsMatcher::from_gix_head recursively walks the HEAD tree on EVERY write_blob_with_path call, even with no .gitattributes anywhere. Callers pay it per file in loops: maw-core merge/build.rs write_blob_at, maw-cli merge.rs patch_candidate_tree, sync/rebase.rs, and (since bn-17o1) maw-git stash_impl worktree_state_commit — the snapshot hot path that runs on every dirty-trunk preserve. Fix: cache the matcher per operation (pass it down or memoize per HEAD oid). Pre-existing cost class, extended by bn-17o1; measure before/after on a snapshot of a few hundred dirty files.","kind":"task","title":"AttrsMatcher::from_gix_head walks full HEAD tree per write_blob_with_path call (N-file snapshot = N walks)"}	blake3:wZHODPG7x6DS05lBH1R0G5BkqtXUpFLWJGJx1FCzoi4
1786824054561236	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyoRY		item.comment	bn-17o1	{"body":"Lead review of d8e31eed (maw-dev): APPROVED. Single-site fix routed through the GitRepo trait method (correct feature-gating: default method falls back to plain write_blob without lfs feature); stash_create/apply audit sound (index entries already post-clean; smudge gap is repo-wide and out of scope); non-user-content write_blob sites correctly left alone. LFS pointer round-trip test is the right proof. Perf finding (per-file HEAD-tree walk) filed as follow-up. Flake matches bn-24xy."}	blake3:LYW_6RPf7pEEHtuMb1z-gG8A5KL0_voAMlDuRNQQORE
1786824075707746	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyohY		item.comment	bn-286g	{"body":"TRIAGED + FIXED (workspace bn-286g, commit 59db6861). NOT a production data-loss bug: no committed work was ever orphaned. The defect is an ORACLE-COMPLETENESS gap in the bn-rah2 escape oracle.\n\n## Reproduced\n`DST_TRACES=48 DST_STEPS=48 cargo test --test dst_production_tier --release --features assurance` fails with 4 SiblingRefFaithfulness violations: seed 0 step 44 (ws-4 blob f9bb17ed, ws-5 blob 999dbc26), seed 15 step 35 (ws-6 b827ca1c), seed 18 step 32 (ws-6 fd0387c6). Extracted each seed's op trace and preserved the post-op repo with a temporary instrumented copy of the harness.\n\n## Extracted shape (seed 0, step 44 = `Merge{srcs:[ws-6], into:default, destroy:false}`)\nPre-op: ws-4 and ws-5 are live, clean, committed-ahead siblings of the epoch (1d527026); neither is a merge source. Post-op the merge advanced the epoch to 93332548 and the sibling auto-rebase replayed both.\n\nBoth siblings' commits WERE replayed (identical messages, ws-4 HEAD 9a1720f5 -> 3c041402 with all 4 commits, ws-5 13f00ea8 -> fb5a9f78). Tree diff old vs new shows exactly one changed path per sibling:\n\n  ws-4/file-1.txt  f9bb17ed -> 3e6e8bdf\n  shared/file-1.txt (ws-5)  999dbc26 -> dba94317\n\nand the new blob is a diff3 CONFLICT-MARKER blob whose header/body contains the old bytes verbatim:\n\n    # structured conflict at ws-4/file-1.txt\n    # side epoch blob: 4a7a318a...\n    # side ws-4 blob: f9bb17ed...\n    <<<<<<< epoch (current) ... ||||||| base ... ======= ... >>>>>>> ws-4 (workspace changes)\n\nand the original OID is pinned on disk in the sibling's sidecar:\n\n    .manifold/artifacts/ws/ws-4/rebase-conflicts.json\n    {\"conflicts\":[{\"path\":\"ws-4/file-1.txt\",\"ours\":\"blob:4a7a318a...\",\"theirs\":\"blob:f9bb17ed...\"}], ...}\n\nAll four violations across all three seeds have this identical shape (seed 15: ws-6/file-0.txt, seed 18: shared/file-0.txt; both pinned in ws-6's rebase-conflicts.json). So: the sibling replay conflicted on a path the sibling had committed, maw rewrote it as conflict-as-data (recoverable via `maw ws resolve` / `maw ws recover`), and NO ref movement lost anything. No ref bug, no misclassification in `reconcile_epoch_with_branch` or `sync_ff_paths_in_worktree`.\n\n## Root cause (file:line)\ncrates/maw-assurance/src/oracle_escape.rs:211 (pre-fix) — `SiblingRefFaithfulness::check_step` reported any tracked blob missing from `git rev-list --objects <frontier>` as `SiblingWorkOrphaned`, with no conflict-as-data carveout.\n\nOracle A has carried exactly that carveout since bn-3g6o (crates/maw-assurance/src/oracle_a.rs:243-305: sidecar OID pin, then containment in a reachable marker blob). The bn-2bcx escape oracles were added later (2026-07) as bare OID-reachability checks and never inherited it. The default 16x24 budget never reaches a CONFLICTING sibling replay, which is why CI stayed green while every deeper run false-failed — the same \"oracle depth ceiling\" class as bn-3g6o, re-found in a different oracle.\n\n## Fix\n`SiblingRefFaithfulness` now applies the same two rescue tests, in the same order, via the SAME helpers — `conflict_sidecar_blobs_for` / `read_blob_bytes` / `reachable_marker_blob_bytes` / `contains_subslice` were promoted to `pub(crate)` in oracle_a rather than re-implemented, so the two oracles cannot drift apart again:\n  (a) the blob OID is pinned as a conflict side in a LIVE workspace's rebase-conflicts.json / conflict-tree.json (live-only: a destroyed workspace's stale sidecar must not rescue);\n  (b) the blob's bytes appear verbatim inside a reachable blob that is itself a conflict-marker blob (nested wrapping).\nBoth computed lazily — a clean step pays nothing. A blob in no reachable tree, no live sidecar and no reachable marker blob still fires.\n\n## Tests (all at DEFAULT budget, so CI catches regressions forever)\n* maw-scenario: `bn_286g_regression_plan()` + `bn_286g_regression_plan_has_expected_shape` (BN_286G_REGRESSION_SEED) — two workspaces commit the same path, one is merged, the sibling replay conflicts.\n* tests/dst_production_tier.rs: `bn_286g_conflicted_sibling_replay_is_green` — drives that plan through the REAL maw binary with TWO non-vacuity assertions (a conflict sidecar was actually written AND a marker blob actually exists), so it cannot pass by never reaching the conflict.\n* crates/maw-assurance/src/oracle_escape.rs unit tests: `conflict_marker_rewrite_with_sidecar_stays_green_bn_286g`, `nested_marker_wrapped_blob_without_sidecar_stays_green_bn_286g` (green twins) + `orphaned_blob_without_sidecar_or_marker_still_trips_bn_286g`, `stale_sidecar_of_destroyed_ws_does_not_rescue_bn_286g` (negative controls).\n\nAcceptance proof: with the carveout locally disabled, `bn_286g_conflicted_sibling_replay_is_green` fails with the exact signature (\"live workspace 'ws-sibling' committed blob 3c10970f... no longer reachable\") and both green twins go RED, while both negative controls stay GREEN.\n\n## Evidence\n* Deep DST re-run post-fix: `dst-production-tier: ran 2304 op-steps across 48 seeds (48 steps/seed); 1274 ops succeeded, 355 workspaces created, 68 epoch advances, 383 Oracle-A witness blobs, 55 ws-advances; 102 out-of-maw-commits, 79 dirty-trunk-writes, 84 gc-runs; 2545 clean-materialization checks; 0 violations over N=2304 trials (Wilson 95% UB = 1.667e-3)` -> `test result: ok. 28 passed; 0 failed; 1 ignored` in 68.72s. Seeds 0/15/18 pass.\n* `maw exec bn-286g -- just check`: exit 0, 89 `test result: ok` lines, ZERO `test result: FAILED`, no errors/warnings.\n\n## Notes / residual risk\n* NO production code changed. If the intent of this bone was also to harden the merge path, the correct follow-up is separate: the conflicted-sibling outcome IS already surfaced (merge prints `CONFLICT: rebased with N conflict(s) ... resolve: maw ws resolve <ws> --list`), so nothing here is silent.\n* Rescue (b) shells out `git cat-file` per reachable object, so it is O(reachable) — but only on a blob that survived neither reachability nor the sidecar pin, and the tracker is refreshed to the current HEAD every step, so it can fire at most once per orphan event. Not on any hot path.\n* Lesson recorded in notes/sg1-dst-architecture.md §7: any NEW content-reachability oracle must consume the shared conflict-as-data rescue, and must be exercised deep enough to reach a conflicting replay.\n* Bone left OPEN, workspace bn-286g left undestroyed, nothing pushed or merged."}	blake3:_TQcnkSXvH4ihIMB3g8A0f5NCjnCLA-9UoYaIvsoCfQ
1786824136447873	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyoxY		item.comment	bn-286g	{"body":"Lead review of 59db6861 (maw-dev): APPROVED. Verdict accepted: oracle-completeness gap, not production data loss — forensic proof (replayed commits present, single conflict-marker blob containing original bytes verbatim, OID pinned in rebase-conflicts.json sidecar) plus acceptance proof (carveout disabled locally reproduces exact signature). Fix correctly SHARES oracle_a's rescue helpers (pub(crate), no reimplementation) with live-sidecar-only rescue and lazy evaluation; Prime Invariant semantics unchanged. Non-vacuous default-budget regression + deep DST 48x48 green (seeds 0/15/18 pass). Downgrading the release-blocking framing: no release blocker remains from this bone."}	blake3:uBF7Y_J6CjvauuczewWQLQXDcDTHbHJ8onUW-qzzWD4
