1786825183008844	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyqRY		item.create	bn-2nhl	{"description":"Found by black-box validation 2026-08-15 (trunk 555aabc9), repos under /tmp/maw-validate/t11.\nThree related failures in the recovery front door:\n1. `maw ws recover --ref <ref> --restore-file <path>` errors \"Default workspace not found at\n   <root>/.maw/workspaces/default\" in the consolidated layout (default = repo root, not\n   .maw/workspaces/default). This is the EXACT command maw itself prints in the bn-1xmk\n   dirty-trunk replay warning — the advertised recovery path for preserved dirty trunk files\n   does not work.\n2. `maw ws recover default --show <path>` / `--restore-file` fail with \"No destroy records\n   found for workspace 'default'\" even though the listing shows a `default ... SOURCE=pinned`\n   row and the footer suggests exactly those commands per row.\n3. Listing shows DIRTY_FILES 0 for a snapshot that preserved 2 dirty files.\nPrime-Invariant adjacent: the snapshots exist and are sound (verified via git show on the\nrecovery ref) — only the tooling to get bytes back out is broken. Fix all three; add\nintegration tests in the consolidated layout for: recover --ref --restore-file to repo root,\nrecover default --show for pinned rows, and DIRTY_FILES count.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["reliability","field-validation"],"title":"ws recover --ref/--restore-file and pinned-row commands broken in consolidated layout","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:PFAa5ZuVItrtRx9lH04Y8ky2Ja-3wyLJeHSpPRkpoLE
1786825183176676	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyqhY		item.create	bn-1ero	{"description":"Found by black-box validation 2026-08-15 (trunk 555aabc9, /tmp/maw-validate/t11). Two halves\nof the same gap (bn-17o1 fixed the CLEAN side only; no smudge path exists in maw-git):\n1. `maw ws recover --ref <ref> --to rescued` materializes an LFS-tracked file as the 129-byte\n   pointer TEXT, not the content, even though the raw bytes are in .git/lfs/objects. Any\n   maw-materialized worktree (recover --to, possibly others) has the same exposure.\n2. Every merge with a dirty LFS-tracked trunk file fires the bn-1xmk warning \"replay did not\n   reproduce your uncommitted edits to '<file>'\" and falls back to the in-memory snapshot —\n   result is CORRECT but the alarm is unconditional noise: the comparison is raw worktree\n   bytes vs the pointer blob. Compare post-clean-filter forms (or smudge before compare).\nFix: add smudge-side materialization (pointer -> content when object present in local store;\nleave pointer + warn when absent) at the worktree-materialization sites, and make the bn-1xmk\nreplay comparison filter-aware. Tests for both, plus recover --to round-trip of an LFS file.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["lfs","field-validation"],"title":"LFS smudge gap: recover/materialize writes pointer bytes; bn-1xmk replay warning spurious for dirty LFS files"}	blake3:KPlppdjoV9AFHHFvlCZ2wY3Vvqbxwd1eL87awLWpj3k
1786825183342962	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyqxY		item.create	bn-154g	{"description":"Found by black-box validation 2026-08-15 (trunk 555aabc9, /tmp/maw-validate/t9). Inject the\nbn-p3m9-style corruption into a clean workspace (stale bytes + stat-cache mask so git status\nis clean), then run `maw ws sync` on the stale workspace: the FF checkout rewrites every file\nso the outcome is correct, BUT no warning, no artifact, and the pre-repair bytes are NEVER\npinned — unlike the FF-absorb site, where bn-3gba pins to a recovery ref before repairing.\nThe bn-3gba verifier at the sync call site runs after the full checkout has already\noverwritten the divergence, so it can never see it. maw destroyed bytes it believed clean\nwithout a snapshot.\nFix: in the sync FF path, BEFORE checkout, run the tree-based divergence check (same helper\nas materialize_verify); if divergence found on a supposedly-clean workspace, pin the current\nworktree state (capture_paths_to_ref pattern) and emit the same WARNING+artifact as the\nFF-absorb site. Keep the fast path cheap: only the tree compare runs when status says clean.\nFailpoint/regression test mirroring the t9 injection shape.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["reliability","field-validation"],"title":"sync FF checkout overwrites hidden worktree divergence without pinning (bn-3gba asymmetry)"}	blake3:fqcW1VXvSc4Rt0rcyi-9fZEXJ865kw18GHJvVXNh3FE
1786825183507515	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyrBY		item.create	bn-34wr	{"description":"Batch of three cosmetic defects from black-box validation 2026-08-15 (trunk 555aabc9):\n1. `maw doctor` prints \"Some checks failed.\" when only [WARN] lines exist; `maw fsck` counts\n   an [INFO] stale-locks line toward \"1 violation(s)\". Both exit 0. Green runs look red —\n   say \"N warning(s)\" / exclude INFO from violation counts.\n2. Append-only refusal message says \"[merge] append_only in .manifold/config.toml\" — wrong\n   path in consolidated layout; should be .maw/manifold/config.toml (or resolve dynamically).\n   Site: crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs:~3354. Audit for other hardcoded\n   .manifold/config.toml mentions in user-facing strings.\n3. `maw merge last-conflict` prints \"recorded 1786825008840 ms UTC\" — format as ISO-8601.\nTests where cheap (string asserts).\n","kind":"task","labels":["ux","field-validation"],"title":"Output polish: doctor/fsck severity wording, append-only message config path, last-conflict raw timestamp"}	blake3:O8DSgycubfUkbdy49un58CMH-A60X-6EAgqwTttlh1g
