1786826120425104	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEytRY		item.comment	bn-34wr	{"body":"Implemented in workspace bn-34wr (commit ef847b82, not merged yet).\n\n1. doctor/fsck severity wording\n   - `maw doctor`: new `summary_line()` helper (crates/maw-cli/src/doctor.rs) distinguishes\n     three cases: all OK -> \"All checks passed!\" (unchanged); any [FAIL] present ->\n     \"Some checks failed. See above for details.\" (unchanged); only [WARN]s -> new\n     \"N warning(s), no failures.\" Exit code was already 0 in all non-fail cases; untouched.\n   - `maw fsck`: `total_violations()` (crates/maw-cli/src/fsck/mod.rs) now excludes\n     Severity::Info from both the text summary (\"N violation(s)\") and the JSON\n     `summary.violations` field, so an INFO-only finding (e.g. stale-locks) no longer\n     inflates the count on a run that exits 0. `exit_code()` already excluded Info from\n     the worst-severity computation (EXIT_CLEAN/WARN/CORRUPTION semantics unchanged) --\n     only the display metric was wrong, now aligned with it. Also loosened the\n     \"Run `maw fsck --repair`\" hint to fire on `repairable > 0` alone (previously gated on\n     the now-filtered `violations > 0`, which could hide a real repair opportunity when\n     the only violation was an Info-severity one).\n\n2. Hardcoded \".manifold/config.toml\" path\n   - append-only refusal message (workspace/merge.rs, was ~line 3354): now resolves via\n     `LayoutFlavor::detect_with_env(root).manifold_dir(root).join(\"config.toml\")` instead\n     of a hardcoded V2 string. Extracted to `append_only_refusal_message()` so it's unit\n     testable without a full BuildPhaseOutput/repo.\n   - Audited all user-facing strings for other hardcoded \".manifold/\" mentions and fixed\n     the ones that would print wrong under the consolidated layout:\n     - epoch_gc.rs: \"No epoch snapshots found in .manifold/epochs.\" -> now prints the\n       actual resolved (layout-aware) epochs dir, relative to root.\n     - workspace/merge.rs: three \"Diagnostics: .manifold/artifacts/merge/.../validation.json\"\n       / \".manifold/quarantine/.../validation.json\" bail! messages -> now build the path\n       from the in-scope `manifold_dir` (already layout-resolved) instead of a hardcoded\n       prefix.\n     - workspace/merge.rs (`merge --abort` refusal): \"remove .manifold/merge-state.json\n       manually\" -> now prints the actual `state_path` already in scope.\n     - maw-core/src/backend/reflink.rs: `ReflinkBackendError::EpochSnapshotMissing` gained\n       a `path: PathBuf` field (was message-only with a hardcoded\n       \".manifold/epochs/e-{epoch}/\" string); Display now prints the real resolved\n       snapshot path.\n     - init.rs: two `InitError`/`BrownfieldInitError::Layout` Display impls said \"failed to\n       create .manifold/ directory\" unconditionally (used for either layout) -> reworded to\n       \"failed to create manifold metadata directory\" (layout-agnostic; not path-specific,\n       so no path plumbing needed).\n     - main.rs: pre-init jj-migration notice said \"bootstrap .manifold/ metadata\" ->\n       reworded generically since at that point in the flow no layout has been chosen yet\n       and default init now produces the consolidated layout.\n   - Left correctly-conditioned or already-correct mentions alone: doctor.rs's own\n     `.manifold/` vs `.maw/manifold/` label is already matched on LayoutFlavor;\n     workspace/capture.rs's error already lists both `ws/`, `.manifold/`, and\n     `.maw/manifold/`; maw-assurance/src/fault.rs's `read_merge_phase` is explicitly\n     documented as a v2-only DST harness helper, not general user output. All other hits\n     were test fixtures / doc-comments, not user-visible.\n\n3. `maw merge last-conflict` timestamp\n   - Added `format_timestamp_millis_iso8601(u64) -> String` in workspace/mod.rs, factored\n     out of the existing `now_timestamp_iso8601()` (which now just calls it with the\n     current time) -- reuses the same days_to_ymd math instead of adding another ad hoc\n     formatter. \"Last conflict (recorded {} ms UTC)\" -> \"Last conflict (recorded {ISO-8601}):\".\n\nTests added (all passing):\n- doctor::tests::summary_line_all_ok / _warnings_only_does_not_say_failed /\n  _single_warning_is_not_pluralized_specially / _failure_present_keeps_current_message\n- fsck::tests::total_violations_excludes_info_severity\n- workspace::merge::tests::append_only_refusal_names_consolidated_config_path /\n  _names_v2_config_path\n- workspace::tests::format_timestamp_millis_iso8601_epoch_zero / _known_instant (uses the\n  exact 1786825008840 ms value from the field report)\n\n`just check` ran synchronously in the workspace to completion: fmt-check, clippy\n(-D warnings), full build, and the entire test matrix (unit + integration + DST gates\ndst_g1..g4/determinism + contract_drift) all green -- grepped the full ~4500-line log\nfor \"test result: FAILED\" / \"error:\" / \"panicked at\": zero hits, every \"test result:\"\nline reads \"ok. ... 0 failed\".\n\nManually smoke-tested against the live repo binary: `maw doctor` now prints\n\"3 warning(s), no failures.\" (previously would have read \"Some checks failed.\");\n`maw fsck` now reports \"171 violation(s)\" (WARN/ERROR only, excluding the 268\npre-existing INFO stale-locks) with exit 1 (EXIT_WARN, correctly reflecting real\nWARN-severity findings already present in this repo, unrelated to bn-34wr).\n\nNot pushed/merged/destroyed per instructions -- workspace bn-34wr left open for review."}	blake3:fDz5t13Wxa6dRdKOcMsLNqW8OX5T0JckwZSfRjS4IVc
1786826160169058	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEythY		item.comment	bn-34wr	{"body":"Lead review of ef847b82 (maw-dev): APPROVED. total_violations now mirrors exit_code's Info-exclusion (consistent pair, tested); doctor summary_line distinguishes warn-only from failures; append-only message resolves real config path via LayoutFlavor (tested both layouts); 7 additional hardcoded-path strings fixed with sensible exemptions (v2-only DST helper, dual-path capture error); ISO-8601 test uses the exact field-report ms value. Display-only risk profile, gate green."}	blake3:7QFRr2LkNpkgdEH_1bHUb0jmi3wTb5CU1VD-3AXgU-8
1786826229261577	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEytxY		item.comment	bn-2nhl	{"body":"Fixed in workspace bn-2nhl @ 3761eebd (not merged). All three failures root-caused and fixed; just check green (0 FAILED, exit 0).\n\nROOT CAUSES\n1. crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/recover.rs:1397 and :1421 (pre-fix) called workspace_path(DEFAULT_WORKSPACE), which is unconditionally <workspaces-dir>/default. In the consolidated layout the default workspace IS the repo root, so both --restore-file forms bailed \"Default workspace not found at <root>/.maw/workspaces/default\". Fix: new layout-aware workspace::default_workspace_path() (mod.rs, uses LayoutFlavor::default_target_path, same helper resolve_workspace_path_for_cd uses), wrapped by recover::default_workspace_worktree().\n2. recover.rs show_file():1159 and restore_file():1415 (pre-fix) used destroy_record::read_latest_record(...).with_context(\"No destroy records found for workspace ...\") — record-only, so pinned rows were rejected. Only restore_to() had the pinned fallback (bn-sdv4). Fix: shared resolve_latest_snapshot() (destroy record first, newest pinned recovery ref second) now used by show_file, restore_file, and restore_to.\n3. recover.rs pinned_only_summaries():105 hardcoded dirty_file_count: 0. Fix: pinned_snapshot_dirty_count() counts the snapshot commit tree delta vs its FIRST parent — correct for git-stash-shaped snapshots (>=2 parents: destroy capture, ws clean, bn-1xmk trunk preserve) and for the bn-1xmk in-memory commit (1 parent, message now the shared const merge::PRE_MERGE_SNAPSHOT_MESSAGE). Head-only pins report 0, matching capture_mode=head_only semantics.\n\nALSO\n- Pinned-row footer + the per-workspace pinned view now advertise --show/--restore-file (they work now); migrate.rs stale comment about \"--to only consults destroy records\" corrected.\n- bn-1xmk warning prints a note that --force is needed when the automatic repair already put your bytes back (the safety gate is otherwise a confusing second failure).\n\nTESTS (crates/maw-cli/tests/recover_front_door_bn_2nhl.rs, 7 tests, all run the strings maw itself printed, parsed from its own output):\n- bn_1xmk_printed_restore_command_works_verbatim — triggers the real bn-1xmk warning deterministically (embedded git dir with no commit makes git add -A, hence snapshot_working_copy, fail -> force-checkout + in-memory repair path), parses the printed Inspect:/Restore: lines and runs both VERBATIM; asserts bytes land in the repo root and no .maw/workspaces/default is invented.\n- recover_ref_restore_file_targets_the_repo_root\n- recover_pinned_row_show_file_works / recover_pinned_row_restore_file_works / recover_pinned_row_restore_file_respects_force_gate\n- recover_listing_counts_pinned_dirty_files (text column + JSON dirty_file_count == 2, and both preserved paths readable via --show)\n- recover_listing_footer_commands_work_verbatim — lifts every \"maw ws recover <name> ...\" line out of the listing footer, substitutes only documented placeholders, runs each.\n\nRISKS\n- pinned_snapshot_dirty_count adds one tree diff per pinned row in the listing (bounded by workspace count).\n- Snapshot-shape detection uses parent count plus the shared pre-merge message const; a head-only pin still reports 0 (unchanged behaviour, never over-reports).\n- Precedence unchanged: a destroy record still wins over a pinned ref for the same name, so a capture_mode=none record still reports \"No snapshot was captured\" rather than falling through to a pinned ref."}	blake3:j4kCbFiuxV2flTuLE1Zt_t7Xm5TxfH5y6GVrdew0z-s
1786826264761769	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyuBY		item.comment	bn-2nhl	{"body":"Lead review of 3761eebd (maw-dev): APPROVED. Root causes confirmed (DEFAULT_WORKSPACE path hardcoded at recover.rs restore paths vs LayoutFlavor resolution; destroy-record-only lookup where only restore_to had the bn-sdv4 pinned fallback; hardcoded dirty_file_count 0). Fix shape right: shared default_workspace_path() + resolve_latest_snapshot() instead of per-command copies; pinned dirty count from first-parent tree delta with head-only pins correctly reporting 0. Test strategy is the gold standard — parses and executes maw's own printed Inspect:/Restore:/footer commands verbatim, incl. a deterministic bn-1xmk trigger. Precedence choice (destroy record wins; capture_mode=none does not fall through) is deliberate and documented — accepted. Gate green."}	blake3:ylG9nvJfwlIjx0waaMpJ0bu4QdZ_tEeLi81fBblVUhc
1786826824405692	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyuRY		item.comment	bn-154g	{"body":"Fixed in workspace bn-154g, commit 6c1eb412 (not merged/pushed).\n\n**Where the check landed.** `crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/sync/checks.rs`, in `sync_worktree_to_epoch_inner`, immediately before `checkout_detach` — after the dirty refusal, after the CAS guard and after the ancestor-refusal guard. Those three all return WITHOUT touching the worktree, so there is nothing to preserve on those paths and no reason to pay the detector's cost there; the guard sits at the exact statement that overwrites bytes. A `sync_ff_cas_skip_pins_nothing` test pins that placement.\n\n**Root cause confirmed.** `checkout_tree` builds the index from the target tree and calls `gix::worktree::state::checkout` with `overwrite_existing = true` and `destination_is_initially_empty = false` — it rewrites EVERY entry, not just the epoch delta. So the post-checkout `verify_clean_materialization` sees a clean tree by construction and can never report the divergence it exists to catch.\n\n**Sharing/refactor of the bn-3gba helpers.** No copies. Three shared helpers were extracted from `verify_clean_materialization` and are used verbatim by both directions: `detect_divergence` (tree compare, status fallback), `pin_divergent_bytes` (wraps `capture_before_materialize_repair`), and `emit_record` (artifact, oplog, WARNING, in that order). `format_divergent_paths` now delegates to a shared `format_paths_capped` alongside a new `format_divergent_pairs` for the refusal message. New public API: `preserve_divergence_before_overwrite() -> PreOverwriteGuard {Proceed, Pinned, Blocked}`. `MaterializeRepairRecord` gains `repair_mode` (`repaired-from-head` / `preserved-before-overwrite`) with `#[serde(default)]`, so pre-bn-154g artifacts still deserialize (pinned by a test).\n\n**Fail-safe.** If divergence is found but the pin FAILS, the guard returns `Blocked` and the sync now REFUSES with the path list, leaving worktree/HEAD/epoch ref untouched. The Prime Invariant is unconditional, and the FF-absorb site's analogue is \"capture fails, skip the repair\"; here the repair IS the checkout, so the equivalent is \"abort the sync\". Detector failures never block: if both the tree compare and the status fallback fail, the guard returns `Proceed`.\n\n**Perf.** Measured on maw's own checkout (1438 files, 37 MB): 121 ms cold, 79 ms warm per tree compare. The clean fast-forward sync now pays it twice (pre-checkout plus the existing post-checkout verify), about 160 ms total. No cheaper precondition was adopted: every status-shaped query is precisely what the mask defeats, so anything short of hashing the bytes can false-negative through it.\n\n**Tests.**\n- `tests/sync_ff_hidden_divergence_bn_154g.rs` (new, default `just check` lane, end-to-end through the real binary): `sync_ff_pins_hidden_divergence_before_checkout`, `clean_sync_pins_nothing_and_says_nothing`, `dirty_sync_still_refuses_and_pins_nothing`.\n- `crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/sync/checks.rs` unit tests: `sync_ff_pins_hidden_divergence_before_checkout`, `sync_ff_clean_workspace_pins_nothing`, `sync_ff_dirty_workspace_still_refuses_and_pins_nothing`, `sync_ff_refuses_when_hidden_divergence_cannot_be_pinned`, `sync_ff_cas_skip_pins_nothing`.\n- `materialize_verify` unit tests: `artifact_without_repair_mode_defaults_to_repaired_from_head`, `preserved_before_overwrite_mode_round_trips`, `pair_and_path_formatters_agree`.\n\nNegative control run: with the guard call replaced by `Proceed`, the e2e test fails with exactly the reported symptom — sync succeeds silently, no WARNING. (Note: that check initially \"passed\" against a stale test binary; `cargo build -p maw-cli` was needed first. The known `just check` stale-binary gotcha.)\n\n**Flake found and fixed in the fixtures (worth knowing repo-wide).** gix compares `ctime.secs` whenever `trust_ctime` is on — `gix_index::entry::stat::Stat::matches` checks it INDEPENDENTLY of `check_stat`, where git's `core.checkStat=minimal` drops ctime entirely. Writing the stale bytes always bumps ctime, so the stat-cache mask only survived while the whole injection landed inside one wall-clock second: green on an idle machine, flaky under a loaded `just check` (it bit once). Both fixtures now set `core.trustCTime=false` alongside `core.checkStat=minimal`, and run the status query twice (the first run can make git write back a refreshed index). 48 parallel runs green afterwards. The existing bn-3gba stat-cache test is not exposed (it asserts the mask via the git CLI and detects via the tree comparison, never via gix status), but anyone writing a new stat-cache fixture that goes through maw's gix dirty check needs this.\n\n**DST oracle: skipped, deliberately.** `oracle_worktree` already arms `Sync (ok)` as clean-expected, so the sync path's OUTCOME is covered. The new observable is the pin, and no DST op can produce hidden divergence — it would need a new stat-cache-mask corruption primitive in the generator, which is not cheap and would be the only op of its kind. Left out; say the word if it should be a follow-up bone.\n\n**Gates.** `just check` PASS (exit 0, 90 `test result: ok`, zero `test result: FAILED`) — run twice. `just sg1-materialize-check` (failpoints lane) PASS.\n\n**Risks.** (1) The `Blocked` refusal is a new way for `maw ws sync` to fail; it needs BOTH hidden divergence AND a capture failure, and the message names the paths and the reason. (2) About 80 ms extra per fast-forward sync, paid per workspace when syncing many. (3) A divergence detected on a `HEAD == epoch` no-op sync now pins and warns where it previously said nothing — correct, since the checkout still rewrites the worktree.\n\nNot merged, not pushed, bone left open."}	blake3:EJxPGKdX0UE52E4fYFwwoJiIqnOW39-X5aAKA-KTZQI
1786826867127035	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyuhY		item.comment	bn-154g	{"body":"Lead review of 6c1eb412 (maw-dev): APPROVED. Guard placement correct (after the three non-mutating refusal paths, immediately before checkout_detach — pinned by test); root cause confirmed (checkout_tree overwrite_existing rewrites every entry, so post-checkout verify is blind by construction); helpers extracted from verify_clean_materialization and reused, no copies; fail-safe semantics right (pin failure => Blocked refusal with worktree untouched; detector failure => Proceed); repair_mode serde-defaulted for old artifacts; negative control proves non-vacuity. Perf measured (~80ms warm per FF sync) and acceptable. The gix trust_ctime-bypasses-check_stat finding is valuable — captured in fixtures. Gate green twice + failpoints lane."}	blake3:M-PpnJmAnNeZCPkRXpc9y2w9vvZFVp7Z_tiI170R280
1786826867299765	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyuxY		item.create	bn-22jy	{"description":"Follow-up from bn-154g (2026-08-15): oracle_worktree covers clean-expected outcomes, but the new preserve-before-overwrite pin (bn-154g) and the bn-3gba repair path are only exercised by failpoint/e2e tests — no DST generator op produces a stat-cache-masked worktree corruption, so the DST can never explore interleavings around it. Add a corruption primitive to the op generator (write stale bytes + mask stat incl. core.trustCTime=false per the bn-154g gix finding: gix compares ctime.secs whenever trust_ctime is on, independent of check_stat). Follow bn-2bcx pattern: default profile byte-identical.","kind":"task","title":"DST: stat-cache-mask corruption primitive so sync/absorb pin-and-warn observables are generator-reachable"}	blake3:09lfshRkyUjrhxcTTppAO0_DkEZ7mmjMBz4ygPCurz0
1786827390497039	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyvBY		item.comment	bn-1ero	{"body":"Fixed both halves in workspace bn-1ero (commit b7ff723c, not merged/pushed).\n\nRoot cause for symptom 1 (recover --to materializes pointer text): the LFS smudge\npass (checkout_impl.rs::smudge_lfs_pointers, used by checkout_tree/checkout_detach/\ncheckout_to_branch/worktree_add -- i.e. every workspace materialization site) opened\nthe local LFS store at repo.git_dir(). For any workspace other than \"default\",\nthat's a linked worktree, whose git_dir() is the private\n<common>/worktrees/<name>/ admin dir -- NOT where LFS objects live\n(<common>/lfs/objects/). Every smudge attempt from inside a non-default workspace\ntherefore always \"missed\" the object, even when it was right there in the shared\nstore, and silently left pointer text (the only signal was an invisible\ntracing::warn! -- no subscriber is installed by default). Confirmed by reproducing\nbyte-for-byte against the preserved /tmp/maw-validate/t11 fixture, and with two new\nmaw-git regression tests that construct a real linked worktree.\n\nThe identical bug existed on the WRITE side (lfs_clean.rs::write_blob_with_path, the\nbn-17o1 clean-filter path) -- content committed from within a non-default workspace\nwas being clean-filtered into a private, invisible-to-everyone-else per-worktree LFS\nstore instead of the shared one. Fixed both call sites: git_dir() -> common_dir().\n\nAdded a smudge pass to the one materializer that bypasses checkout_tree entirely:\nmaw ws recover --restore-file reads a snapshot blob and writes it straight to disk.\nAdded maybe_smudge(): pointer -> content when present in the local store (via\ncommon_dir), leaves the pointer + prints a visible WARNING when absent. Also added a\npost-\"--to\"/\"--ref --to\" audit pass (warn_unresolved_lfs_pointers) that prints one\nWARNING per still-pointer path after populate_from_snapshot, since checkout_tree's\nown smudge failure is otherwise silent in normal CLI usage.\n\nAudited and exempted: --show/--search (intentionally read raw git object content,\nmatching real git show/git grep behavior on LFS pointers -- not a materializer);\nresolve.rs/resolve_structured.rs conflict UI (LFS files are -text merge=lfs, routed\nthrough the binary merge driver, not the textual diff3/resolve machinery these\ntouch).\n\nRoot cause for symptom 2 (spurious bn-1xmk warning): confirmed via full\nmaw ws merge reproduction with a genuinely-edited dirty LFS trunk file.\nverify_trunk_replay_fidelity compared raw pre-merge worktree bytes (smudged real\ncontent) against raw post-replay worktree bytes (the committed pointer blob,\nwritten near-verbatim by the replay path for a committed-unchanged file) and fired\nthe warning on every dirty LFS file even when nothing was lost. Fix: normalize both\nsides through the same clean filter write_blob_with_path uses and compare the\nresulting blob OIDs (trunk_replay_content_matches) instead of raw bytes. Kept the\nrepair action unconditional (worktree must always end up holding real content, not\na pointer stub) but made the loud WARNING+recovery-pointer conditional on the\nnormalized OIDs actually differing -- so a real content edit that the replay somehow\ndropped is still caught and still alarms.\n\nTests: 2 new maw-git tests (checkout_impl.rs) building a real linked worktree +\ncommon LFS store to prove the smudge fix and its missing-object fallback; 1 new\nmaw-git test (lfs_clean.rs) proving the write-side fix stores into common_dir from\na linked worktree; 4 new maw-cli unit tests (merge.rs) for\ntrunk_replay_content_matches (pointer==real-content match, genuine-edit still\nflagged, absence/presence asymmetry, non-LFS unaffected); 3 new maw-cli unit tests\n(recover.rs) for maybe_smudge. All new tests independently verified to fail against\nthe pre-fix code (reverted each fix locally, confirmed red, restored). Full\nend-to-end manual repro against a scratch fixture modeled on /tmp/maw-validate/t11:\nrecover --to round-trips real content byte-identically; recover --to with the object\nremoved from .git/lfs/objects leaves the pointer and prints a visible WARNING; a\nreal maw ws merge with a genuinely-edited dirty LFS trunk file produces no bn-1xmk\nwarning and the final worktree holds the real edited content, not a pointer.\n\njust check (fmt + clippy -D warnings + build + full test suite) is clean --\n89 \"test result: ok\" blocks, 0 FAILED, exit 0.\n\nResidual risk / follow-up: while chasing the e2e repro I found gix's\nstatus_head_to_worktree() does NOT flag a smudged-real-content-vs-committed-pointer\ndivergence as dirty when the index's stat cache was rebuilt without going through a\nreal checkout (e.g. after unstage_all's tree-based index rebuild followed by a raw\noverwrite onto the worktree file, outside of any maw operation) -- first repro\nattempt silently found zero dirty entries this way. A real edit via a genuine maw\nworkflow (create workspace, edit tracked file, merge) reproduces the bug correctly\nand my fix handles it; flagging the status blind spot as a separate, not-yet-filed\nobservation in case it matters for other LFS-adjacent invariants (didn't investigate\nroot cause, out of scope here)."}	blake3:fJmKokP-qYlrqmFpXM7S25qCtc01y23Y5GbcYuP3o_0
1786827428556865	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyvRY		item.comment	bn-1ero	{"body":"Lead review of b7ff723c (maw-dev): APPROVED. Root cause stronger than the bone's framing: Store::open(git_dir()) vs common_dir() broke LFS store resolution for ALL linked worktrees — smudge AND the bn-17o1 clean side; both fixed with linked-worktree regression tests. recover --restore-file gets maybe_smudge (bypasses checkout_tree), --to gets a visible unresolved-pointer warning; bn-1xmk replay compare normalizes through the clean filter with the WARNING now conditional on genuine mismatch while the repair stays unconditional. Revert-and-fail verification on every fix. Gate green. Residual gix status observation noted on the bone."}	blake3:HP55TWIM-JnCWPgfpgqapKl5QiCxIvO6VmUhvNnBMdo
1786827978706013	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyvhY		item.move	bn-2nhl	{"state":"done"}	blake3:yRCcn9p5Ug_h06l97pzceP0rtDeEd8fs9nJO6TrzLjE
1786827978739910	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyvxY		item.move	bn-1ero	{"state":"done"}	blake3:ugc3ll5fiNQbd9q8hRi3gjZBX-hDPtNalswk5e7YXn4
