1786828478310404	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEywhY		item.create	bn-17lm	{"description":"Cosmetic, found in validation round 2 (2026-08-15, /tmp/maw-validate2/s5c): the materialize/divergence WARNING text is printed once to stdout and once to stderr, so shells merging streams show it twice. Verified by capturing streams separately — not a duplicate-print bug. Pick one stream (stderr, matching NOTE convention from bn-1du0) for warnings.","kind":"task","title":"sync/materialize WARNING emitted on both stdout and stderr (doubles under 2>&1)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:sxpHqVVf_ggdTZzwjeQMhiiZaIt2GLqVhukDkhgwA2c
1787155346594320	sigil-dev	itc:v3:AWLOeSZkkyTnmRAAAAAAQd3q2q1d7QAAAAExCg		item.create	bn-2fto	{"description":"## Symptom\n\nA dirty (uncommitted) agent workspace was auto-advanced across an epoch when a sibling merged. A file modified in the workspace (src/run_cli.rs) kept the workspace's working copy wholesale. The epoch's new hunks in that same file (from the sibling merge) were dropped silently. No conflict was reported. The worker then committed, producing a commit that reverts the sibling's changes.\n\n## Repro (sigil repo, 2026-08-19)\n\n1. `maw ws create bn-1wzr --from main` at epoch 8b6aaff. Worker edits src/run_cli.rs (uncommitted).\n2. Lead merges sibling bn-2kv4 (2973cce) which also edits src/run_cli.rs (doc comments + 7 tests). `maw ws merge` prints \"INVARIANT: verified 2 sibling workspace(s) — no committed work orphaned\".\n3. Worker keeps working, commits 90b8403. Its parent is now ab8c83b (post-sibling epoch) — so maw advanced the dirty worktree.\n4. `git show 90b8403 -- src/run_cli.rs` contains removals of every line bn-2kv4 added to that file: the worker's commit silently reverts the sibling's work.\n5. `maw ws history bn-1wzr` shows only `[create] (epoch 8b6aaff)` and a later `[rebase] ab8c83b→01e634c` — the dirty-tree advance 8b6aaff→ab8c83b is not recorded as an operation.\n\n## Expected\n\nEither 3-way merge the working-tree changes onto the new epoch (and mark conflicts like sync does for committed work), or refuse to advance a dirty worktree and leave it at the old epoch (the \"Skipping auto-sync to preserve committed work\" path), or at minimum record the advance in `maw ws history` and warn. Silent file-level \"ours\" is data loss that only surfaces at review time (the diff vs main shows removals the worker never made).\n\n## Workaround used\n\n`git show <sibling-commit> -- <file> | git apply --3way` inside the workspace, then commit.","kind":"bug","title":"ws: dirty workspace auto-advanced across an epoch keeps working copy wholesale, silently dropping the epoch's hunks in the same file"}	blake3:e4osScVlMAaXiaDn1zG4phES88XpP06V2KZWLlIpElE
