1787166529096350	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyzxY		item.comment	bn-24xy	{"body":"Root cause confirmed (NOT git 2.55-specific, contrary to prior belief): test setup used `git worktree add --force --detach wt c2` to advance an already-populated linked worktree (wt exists with file1.txt from setup at c1). git's check_candidate_path() in builtin/worktree.c does: if (file_exists(path) && !is_empty_dir(path)) die(\"'%s' already exists\"), unconditionally on --force. --force only covers 'branch checked out elsewhere' / reusing a registered-but-missing worktree admin dir, never an existing non-empty directory. Verified this check is identical (same code) in git 2.17.0 (2018), 2.30.0 (2020), and 2.55.0 (2026 upstream master release notes/source) -- so it was never a --force semantics change in 2.55. The test has been broken since its introduction (f491c581, bn-8flz) and simply hadn't been run against a git build that hit this path in CI/dev machines that produced older leftover binaries/caches, or was previously masked. Fix: test-only change, advance the worktree in place via `git -C wt checkout --force <commit>` instead of re-running worktree add -- correct semantics for the intent, stable across git versions old and new. No product code changed; checkout_detach's stale-tracked-file removal was already correct. cargo test -p maw-git: 63 passed, 0 failed. Full 'just check': all suites green (grepped full ~4000-line log for 'test result: FAILED' -- zero hits). Committed in workspace bn-24xy as 2545e948."}	blake3:KEzpyQqd4lWOb1VpQBsmPIBQmztvCQe48D2CxcSFlKE
1787166559121201	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy0BY		item.move	bn-24xy	{"state":"done"}	blake3:7DOgyxBk1vyFupH1FXJH3L1bRW4EODLMFcRr2dUiDuI
1787166689841746	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy0RY		item.comment	bn-2fps	{"body":"FIXED (workspace bn-2fps, commit 50619d08).\n\nDESIGN: memoized the AttrsMatcher on GixRepo — new field `attrs_cache: RefCell<Option<AttrsCache>>` (cfg(feature=\"lfs\")), keyed by `AttrsKey` = { Pending | Head(Option<ObjectId>) } where the OID is HEAD's TREE oid. write_blob_with_path now calls resolve_attrs() which returns an Rc<AttrsMatcher>, rebuilding only when the key changes. RefCell costs nothing in bounds: gix::Repository is already !Sync (RefCell buffer free-lists), GixRepo was never Sync, and the GitRepo trait carries no Send/Sync bound — no rayon/parallel use of GixRepo anywhere.\n\nSemantics preserved exactly: same 3-tier priority (pending override -> HEAD tree -> workdir fallback), and every former early-return-raw-blob failure path now yields an empty matcher, which is behaviourally identical (is_lfs()==false -> plain write_blob). Replaced from_gix_head with an explicit head_tree_oid() + from_gix_tree so the key and the build read the same tree.\n\nINVALIDATION (documented on AttrsCache):\n- HEAD moves -> new tree OID -> rebuild. Content-addressed, so exact: same tree oid ⇒ byte-identical .gitattributes. A caller that commits a new .gitattributes sees the new rules on its next call.\n- set_pending_gitattributes / clear_pending_gitattributes (&mut self) clear the cache.\n- Working-tree writes are the one thing the OID key cannot see (workdir fallback reads .gitattributes off disk). Added `GixRepo::invalidate_attrs_cache(&self)` and call it at the top of checkout_impl::checkout_tree. Only matters when HEAD's tree has no .gitattributes AND HEAD does not move. Audited the blob-write loops (merge.rs patch_candidate_tree/trunk_replay_content_matches, sync/rebase.rs, stash_impl worktree_state_commit, recover.rs, maw-core merge/build.rs) — all are pure tree-building loops with no interleaved worktree writes.\n\nMEASURED (cargo test --release -p maw-git --test attrs_cache_perf -- --ignored, new #[ignore]d timing harness crates/maw-git/tests/attrs_cache_perf.rs; times whole worktree_state_commit on an all-dirty repo):\n\n  files  .gitattributes   before      after     speedup\n  300    none             119.6 ms    11.4 ms   10.5x\n  300    root file         65.9 ms    11.0 ms    6.0x\n  2000   none              2.828 s    74.5 ms   38.0x\n  2000   root file        775.7 ms    80.9 ms    9.6x\n\nThe 'none' column is the worst case pre-fix because an empty HEAD result also triggered a full recursive WORKDIR walk per file — 2N repo-sized walks. Second run after the fix was stable (74.5/78.9 ms, 11.4/12.3 ms).\n\nTESTS ADDED (crates/maw-git/src/lfs_clean.rs):\n- attrs_matcher_is_built_once_per_head_tree — 25 writes on one HEAD => exactly 1 build; then a commit widening the rules => exactly 2 builds AND the rebuilt matcher actually applies the new *.dat rule (cat-file shows a real LFS pointer); a further write on the unchanged new HEAD stays at 2.\n- pending_gitattributes_override_invalidates_cache — set => rebuild (and a.dat becomes a pointer), cached across writes, clear => rebuild back to HEAD's rules (same oid as before).\n- no_gitattributes_anywhere_is_cached_and_writes_raw_blobs — the common case: 11 writes => 1 build, blob identical to write_blob().\nCounting uses a #[cfg(test)] thread_local build counter in lfs_clean.rs (no public API surface added for it).\n\nCHECK: `just check` fully green — fmt, clippy -D warnings (workspace, all-targets), cargo test, cargo test -p maw-cli, DST harness, contract_drift. 91 'test result: ok' lines, zero 'test result: FAILED'. just check does NOT cover maw-git/maw-lfs, so ran those separately: maw-lfs conformance 5/5, attrs_proptest 7/7, maw-git integration_test 63/63, maw-git lib 53 passed / 1 failed — the failure is the known-environmental checkout_impl::tests::checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files (bn-24xy, git 2.55 'git worktree add --force --detach'), untouched by this change."}	blake3:VZs49wNPU3ovCb-FOE0EalN4CHg-uFcq-vFpC7WAw-E
1787166744858633	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy0hY		item.move	bn-2fps	{"state":"done"}	blake3:hkhUqmf0p27pU6A7wL_4YSxLH7xFqsED7_MisaTESRE
1787166828348401	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy0xY		item.comment	bn-2fto	{"body":"Verified the field scenario on trunk 4537c51e + fixed the history gap (workspace bn-2fto, commit 3bfcd05a).\n\nBLACK-BOX REPRO (scripts+logs: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-bob-src-maw/c2760e00-.../scratchpad/bn-2fto/, scratch repos, installed maw 1.0.0-pre.13 then the rebuilt binary):\n(a) 1-epoch, EXACT field shape (ws A dirty on F.txt head hunk at E0; sibling B commits F.txt tail hunk; lead merges B -> E1; A commits): PASS. A never advances — merge prints 'wsa — skipped: dirty' (post-merge sibling auto-rebase), A's HEAD stays at E0, A's commit parents on E0 and reverts none of B's hunks, A's uncommitted edit preserved verbatim. 'maw exec' also refuses to auto-sync ('WARNING: Workspace is behind the current epoch, but has uncommitted changes. Skipping auto-sync to preserve uncommitted work.').\n(a2) 1-epoch FF-ABSORB shape (dirty path inside the global ff_paths): PASS — the merge REFUSES outright: 'Error: Target branch main has diverged from the current epoch. ... Affected workspace(s): wsa' (pre-existing evaluate_ff_safety guard; covered by tests/merge_ff_absorb.rs::ff_absorb_blocks_when_workspace_touches_ff_path).\n(b) 2-epoch (bn-mq3b): PASS — 'wsa: left stale (NOT fast-forwarded) — 1 uncommitted path(s) also changed in the absorbed epoch(s): F.txt — commit or stash them, then run: maw ws sync wsa'; HEAD unchanged; next commit reverts nothing.\n(c) dirty path DISJOINT from the epoch: PASS, no regression — sibling still FF-advances, epoch-B and absorbed-range content materialized, A's uncommitted file untouched.\n=> the data-loss half of bn-2fto is closed on trunk; nothing further to fix there.\n\nHISTORY GAP (Expected item 3) WAS REAL and is now fixed. Evidence pre-fix: variant (c) advanced wsa's HEAD 36f32c21->08eead77 during the merge and 'maw ws history wsa' showed ONLY '[create]'. FF-absorb replays already recorded (rebase_workspace_run -> record_rebase_op, trigger absorb:ff(..)); FF-absorb fast-forwards and skips recorded nothing. Auto-rebase's SkippedDirty records nothing either (record_rebase_notice returns None for all Skipped* variants) — left as is: nothing moves and the merge output already names it; recording it would add an op per merge per dirty sibling.\nChanges (crates/maw-cli): merge.rs — SiblingClass now carries base_epoch/head_before; FF advance records OpPayload::Rebase (0 replayed, trigger absorb:ff(..)) only when HEAD actually moved; SkipStaleDirty records OpPayload::Annotate key 'ff-absorb-skipped' with reason/old_epoch/new_epoch/trigger/stale_paths/summary (Annotate keeps the oplog schema additive, same rationale as materialize_verify repair records). sync/rebase.rs — record_rebase_op made pub. history.rs + ops_log.rs — an Annotate carrying a 'summary' string renders it inline.\nNow: '[rebase] rebase 02bee900→84142805 (0 commit(s)) [absorb:ff(c51318ef64ee..84142805f864)]' and '[annotate] annotate: ff-absorb-skipped — left stale at 02bee900 (not fast-forwarded to 84142805): 1 uncommitted path(s) also changed in the absorbed epoch(s): F.txt'.\n\nTESTS: new crates/maw-cli/tests/ff_absorb_stale_sibling_cli.rs::dirty_sibling_editing_the_merged_file_is_not_advanced_no_silent_revert (variant (a) end-to-end; the 1-epoch shape had no coverage — tests/auto_rebase_siblings.rs only covered a dirty sibling with a DISJOINT private file); history assertions added to the two existing FF-absorb tests; history.rs unit test summarize_annotate_payload_with_summary_detail.\n'just check' GREEN (exit 0, 91 'test result: ok', zero 'test result: FAILED'/'error'/panics). bn-24xy's checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files did not appear in this run's output at all."}	blake3:OaAgZ9mYOzriMhpAZ92Iob6xWuzQEdAyZ5-fJH0R9ms
1787166875207312	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy1BY		item.move	bn-2fto	{"state":"done"}	blake3:Ld7GElpGuRGlWbItcgRhDC6EuD0UJ29ntdJh5BRPfkA
1787168037750044	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy1RY		item.comment	bn-22jy	{"body":"SHIPPED in ws bn-22jy @ 73b3452a.\n\nOP: `Op::CorruptWorktreeStatMasked { ws, path: Option<String>, nonce: u64 }` (maw-scenario). Driver resolves the victim against the real HEAD tree (hint, else first tracked non-empty file currently equal to its HEAD blob), writes a nonce-derived SAME-LENGTH ASCII payload, and forges the stat cache: core.checkStat=minimal + core.trustctime=false (the bn-154g gix finding), back-date mtime -> reset --mixed HEAD -> update-index --refresh -> write stale -> re-apply mtime -> confirm 'git status --porcelain' empty TWICE. Mask failure restores the original bytes and returns None (no half-corrupted fixture). Mask holds reliably on ext4.\n\nPROFILE FLAG: `ConditionProfile::corrupt_weight` (#[serde(default)] 0) + `with_corrupt_weight()`. Separate knob from escape_weight on purpose.\n\nBYTE-IDENTICAL PROOF (op-stream FNV-1a over plan.steps, seeds 0..256 x 128 steps; pristine trunk 4537c51e generator extracted via 'git show' into a scratch crate vs the patched one):\n  default            0x61c78834e645f514 == 0x61c78834e645f514\n  prodtier(adv8,esc3)0x7353896eacca2728 == 0x7353896eacca2728\n  adv8/esc8          0xceffff94f36bdfd6 == 0xceffff94f36bdfd6\n  +corrupt10         0x839da2b88452aa65 (differs -> knob is not a no-op)\nPinned permanently as DEFAULT_PROFILE_OP_STREAM_DIGEST / PRODUCTION_TIER_OP_STREAM_DIGEST / ESCAPE_HEAVY_OP_STREAM_DIGEST with tests default_profile_op_stream_digest_is_pinned + gated_profiles_op_stream_digests_are_pinned.\n\nORACLES: new `MaskedStalePreservation` (oracle_worktree) — once masked bytes leave the disk they MUST be reachable from refs/manifold/recovery/<ws>/*. `CleanMaterialization` gains a masked_stale set, excluded from the assertion and re-armed only when the worktree is OBSERVED clean again (plan-level guesses all produced false positives: git add -A trusts the forged stat cache, and a no-op sync exits 0 without touching the worktree).\n\nTESTS: maw-scenario 25 pass (5 new bn_22jy_tests); maw-assurance 112 pass (5 new oracle unit tests incl. RED/GREEN twins); dst_production_tier 30 pass incl. new bn_154g_masked_stale_pin_is_green (deterministic corrupt->epoch-bump->sync trace; asserts the exact refs/manifold/recovery/ws-victim/materialize-* pin) and dst_production_tier_masked_stale_corruption (8x16 default, green at 16x24 too). LOAD-BEARING PROOF: neutering preserve_divergence_before_overwrite to Proceed turns bn_154g_masked_stale_pin_is_green RED with 'MaskedStalePreservation: merge overwrote the stat-cache-masked bytes at ws-victim/base.txt ... reachable from no recovery ref'. `just check` EXIT=0, 91 'test result: ok', zero FAILED.\n\nFINDING FOR TRIAGE (not fixed here): at 8x16 the oracle initially fired 4x on op=destroy — 'maw ws destroy' removes a workspace whose masked-stale bytes are in no recovery snapshot, because the destroy snapshot is built from git state and the forged stat cache hides them. Same class as bn-154g at a different site with a different contract. Oracle is now scoped to overwrites of a LIVE workspace and counts the carve-out (destroyed_unjudged) so it is visible, not swallowed. Worth its own bone.\n\nALSO: reaching the bn-154g guard needs corrupt BEFORE the epoch bump — a merge auto-rebases every clean sibling itself, so a trailing 'maw ws sync' reports 'up to date' and never touches the worktree. sync_worktree_to_epoch_inner serves both the CLI and the auto-rebase, so the guard is covered either way."}	blake3:jO2FCZfYsIxL-f4HShMcfAoRuiDFjNE5dBdk6o9P28k
1787168239066030	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy1hY		item.move	bn-22jy	{"state":"done"}	blake3:EqHkh4c1Q9OZnaPS2VadhTpFZ4TCOFArirnCm0u5GjI
1787168269801746	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy1xY		item.create	bn-2k9e	{"description":"Found by the bn-22jy DST corruption primitive (2026-08-19), same class as bn-154g at a different site.\n\n## Symptom\n`maw ws destroy <ws>` (and merge `--destroy`) builds its recovery snapshot from git state. When a workspace holds a stat-cache-masked stale file (on-disk bytes differ from HEAD but `(size, mtime)` match the index entry and `core.trustCTime=false`/ctime also matches, so every status-shaped query — git status, gix status_head_to_worktree — reports CLEAN), the snapshot omits those bytes and the destroy removes the worktree. The divergent bytes are then reachable from NO `refs/manifold/recovery/<ws>/*` ref. That is the exact blind spot bn-154g closed for `sync`'s FF checkout (`preserve_divergence_before_overwrite`), but destroy's snapshot path has no equivalent pre-removal hash-compare.\n\n## Evidence\nAt 8x16 with `corrupt_weight>0` the `MaskedStalePreservation` oracle (crates/maw-assurance/src/oracle_worktree.rs) fired 4x on `op=destroy`. The oracle was scoped to overwrites of a LIVE workspace and the destroy case is reported via a visible `destroyed_unjudged` counter (not silently ignored) pending this bone.\n\n## Expected\nDestroy's snapshot (worktree_state_commit / destroy record) should hash-compare tracked files against HEAD blobs (not trust the stat cache) before removal, mirroring bn-154g — or at minimum pin the divergent bytes to `refs/manifold/recovery/<ws>/materialize-*` with a warning — then drop the `destroyed_unjudged` carve-out so the oracle judges destroy too.\n\n## Repro\n`cargo test --release --features assurance --test dst_production_tier dst_production_tier_masked_stale_corruption` after removing the destroy carve-out in oracle_worktree.rs; or hand-build: corrupt per `corrupt_worktree_stat_masked` in tests/dst_production_tier.rs, then `maw ws destroy <ws>` and `maw ws recover <ws> --show <path>`.\n","kind":"bug","title":"destroy recovery snapshot is blind to stat-cache-masked stale worktree bytes (bn-154g class at destroy site)"}	blake3:85_rX0VFMOMF_rJ03GKNTClZOfzfKD5Lnq_1b8lVv18
1787330700151829	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy2BY		item.move	bn-2k9e	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:3GU2kOqidLaFLXIRUbN_XmSTjMzUP8WuLd81xVOR818
1787330700156728	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy2RY		item.assign	bn-2k9e	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-dev"}	blake3:vjnjK4W6FueEmPAwfgvkciEWzo7en8UMlO-obFP-az8
1787332902314555	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy2hY		item.comment	bn-2k9e	{"body":"SHIPPED in ws bn-2k9e @ 6dcace0d (not merged).\n\nROOT CAUSE. Destroy's recovery snapshot is built from two stat-cache-trusting\nsteps, and BOTH miss a masked file:\n1. `capture::list_dirty_paths` (gix `status_head_to_worktree`) decides *whether*\n   there is anything to snapshot and what `dirty_files` the destroy record lists;\n2. `capture_dirty_worktree`'s `git add -A` decides *which bytes* land in the\n   stash tree — `git add` (with or without `-f`) also consults the index stat\n   cache, so a masked entry is staged as its HEAD blob even when some OTHER file\n   drags the destroy onto the dirty-capture path.\nOn top of that, `create::destroy()` only called the capture at all under\n`--force`, and the same mask makes `compute_patchset`'s `git diff <epoch>`\nreport 0 touched files — so the unmerged-changes refusal never fires and the\nloss needs no `--force`. Measured directly: `git add -A` on the real index\nstages `HEADCONTENT-ORIGINAL` for a same-length-masked file; `read-tree HEAD`\ninto a fresh index (zeroed stat) + `add -A`, `add --renormalize`, and\n`update-index --force-remove` + `add -f` all stage the real `STALE-...` bytes.\n\nFIX (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/capture.rs).\n* `hidden_divergent_paths()` runs bn-154g's detector REUSED VERBATIM\n  (`materialize_verify::divergent_paths_by_tree`, promoted to `pub(crate)`) —\n  throwaway index from HEAD (zeroed stat) + `git add -A` + `diff-tree` — minus\n  the paths the caller already captures, minus paths absent from disk.\n  Deliberately NOT `detect_divergence`: its fallback is the status query, which\n  is exactly what the mask defeats.\n* `capture_before_destroy` unions the hidden paths into the reported dirty set\n  and passes them as `force_rehash` to `capture_dirty_worktree`, which now calls\n  `force_rehash_paths` (`git update-index --force-remove` + `git add -f`,\n  chunked 256) BEFORE `stage_all_for_capture`, so `git add -A` has no forged\n  stat entry left to trust. Covers `ws merge --destroy`, `undo`, `migrate` and\n  the rewrite/replay path for free.\n* `capture_hidden_stale_before_destroy` is the new non-`--force` entry point.\n  It pins into the ORDINARY destroy namespace (`RefKind::Destroy` ->\n  `refs/manifold/recovery/<ws>/<ts>`), not `materialize-*`, on purpose: the\n  destroy record then points at it, so `maw ws recover <ws> --show <path>`,\n  `--restore-file` and `--search` all resolve the masked bytes through the\n  normal front door with ZERO changes to recover.rs / DestroyRecord.\n* Loud stderr WARNING naming <=5 paths + the `maw ws recover <ws> --show`\n  recovery command.\n* `create::destroy()`'s snapshot-reporting block is re-keyed on the capture\n  rather than on `--force` (the \"(nothing to snapshot)\" wording is preserved for\n  clean `--force` and pinned by a test).\n\nFAIL-CLOSED. Per-file: an unreadable file makes `git add -A` fail, so the\ndetector fails, so the widened path force-rehashes it too and `git add -f`\nfails -> capture Err -> destroy aborts. Detector failure as a whole: `--force`\nwidens `rehash` to every tracked file (`git ls-files -z`; the capture still\nreturns None when nothing actually differs, so a clean workspace pins nothing);\nnon-force REFUSES with \"re-run with --force\". Pin failure mid-destroy: the\ncapture is the FIRST destructive-path step — `Err` propagates before\n`write_destroy_record` and before `backend.destroy`, and merge --destroy's\nexisting arm preserves the workspace for manual cleanup. To keep that refusal\nfrom regressing ordinary repos, `divergent_paths_by_tree` gained the\nembedded-repo `:(exclude)` retry `stage_all_for_capture` already had (git\nadd -A fails outright on a git dir without a checked-out commit); this also\nupgrades bn-154g's sync guard from its status fallback in that case.\n\nLFS / FILTER-AWARENESS. Both the detector and the rehash go through `git add`,\nwhich runs the configured clean filter — verified empirically: HEAD holding an\nLFS pointer while the worktree holds smudged bytes yields an EMPTY diff-tree.\nUnit test `lfs_pointer_in_head_vs_smudged_worktree_is_not_divergence` (skips\nwhen git-lfs is not configured, where the bytes genuinely differ from HEAD and\npinning them is correct-if-noisy — the same property bn-154g's sync guard\nalready ships).\n\nORACLE. `MaskedStalePreservation`'s `destroyed_unjudged` carve-out is GONE\n(field, accessor, `!ws_dir.is_dir()` early-return, type docs, and the\n`masked_destroyed_unjudged` counter + report string in tests/dst_production_\ntier.rs). A removed workspace now falls through the same \"bytes are no longer\non disk\" check, so destroy is held to the same reachability contract as an\noverwrite. Unit tests replaced by a RED/GREEN twin:\n`destroyed_workspace_without_a_pin_is_a_violation` /\n`destroyed_workspace_with_a_pin_is_clean`.\n\nTESTS.\n* NEW tests/destroy_hidden_divergence_bn_2k9e.rs (default `just check` lane, real\n  binary): destroy_snapshots_stat_masked_stale_bytes (no --force; asserts the\n  WARNING, exactly one pin, `git show <ref>:victim` == STALE, `maw ws recover\n  alice --show` == STALE, record capture_mode=dirty_snapshot naming the path,\n  and `maw ws recover --search`), force_destroy_keeps_masked_bytes_alongside_\n  visible_dirt, merge_destroy_snapshots_stat_masked_stale_bytes,\n  clean_destroy_pins_nothing_and_says_nothing (EXACT stdout match +\n  capture_mode=none + dirty_files=[] + snapshot_ref=null + no refs),\n  clean_force_destroy_reports_nothing_to_snapshot.\n* capture.rs unit tests: capture_before_destroy_snapshots_stat_masked_stale_\n  bytes, capture_hidden_stale_pins_into_the_destroy_namespace,\n  capture_hidden_stale_on_a_clean_workspace_pins_nothing,\n  lfs_pointer_in_head_vs_smudged_worktree_is_not_divergence,\n  hidden_divergent_paths_excludes_already_captured_paths.\n\nLOAD-BEARING PROOF (negative controls, `hidden_divergent_paths` neutered to\nreturn empty). e2e: the three positive tests go RED with \"exactly one destroy\npin expected, got: []\" — i.e. the bytes are reachable from no recovery ref —\nwhile both clean controls stay green. DST at 8x16: 5 violations (4 on\nop=destroy, 1 on op=merge, i.e. --destroy), e.g. \"'destroy' removed the\nstat-cache-masked bytes at 'ws-2/base.txt' ... reachable from no\nrefs/manifold/recovery/ws-2/* ref\". With the fix: 0.\n\nGATES. `just check` EXIT=0, 92 \"test result: ok\", zero FAILED, zero\nerror/panicked. dst_production_tier (release, assurance) 30 passed. masked-stale\nlane green at 8x16 (7 masked-removal judgements) and 16x24 (13 judgements, 20\neffective corruptions), 0 violations. maw-git 54 / maw-lfs 63 / maw-scenario 25\ngreen; maw-assurance --features oracles 113 passed (was 112). clippy\n--workspace --all-targets clean.\n\nPERF. Destroy now pays one content hash of the worktree: 70-80 ms warm on maw's\nown checkout (1441 files / 37 MB), gitignored trees pruned. Paid on EVERY\ndestroy including clean ones and once per workspace in `ws merge --destroy` —\ndestroy is not a hot path, and nothing cheaper can see through the mask (every\nstatus-shaped query is precisely what it defeats). No AttrsMatcher/bn-2fps hot\npath is involved: the comparison is one `git add -A`, not a per-file walk.\n\nRISKS. (1) New non-force refusal when the hash comparison cannot run (broken git\nplumbing in the worktree); `--force` still works and takes the widened capture.\n(2) A non-force destroy can now print a snapshot banner and pin a ref where it\npreviously printed one line — only when real hidden divergence exists.\n(3) In a repo with `filter=lfs` attributes but no git-lfs clean filter\nconfigured, every smudged LFS file reads as divergence and would be pinned\n(safe, but heavy). Same property as bn-154g's sync guard; worth a follow-up if\nit ever bites."}	blake3:8NJo4kKw7ZAh2iUtDdnA7kN-rHO5MePdF8ILfTzJpbY
